{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-5144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+({y}^{2}-6y) & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}) & =3+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+9) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-2,3)$ and its radius is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a258d3a2e0e27b7c226e21ede81ca9fb0a114c45cb76137c083288ea969fc75"} {"question" "q-5144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-2,3)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(2,-3)$, radius: $16$"] ["text" "center: $(2,-3)$, radius: $4$"] ["text" "center: $(3,-2)$, radius: $16$"] ["text" "center: $(3,-2)$, radius: $8$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(-2,3)$, radius: $4$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3y & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}-3y) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and its radius is $\\frac{3}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a258d3a2e0e27b7c226e21ede81ca9fb0a114c45cb76137c083288ea969fc75"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(0,-\\frac{3}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(0,\\frac{1}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{5}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(0,\\frac{9}{4})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-5195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A circle in the Cartesian plane is given by the equation $8x+{x}^{2}-2y=64-{y}^{2}.$ If the circle is written in the standard form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2},$ then $a+b+r=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the standard form of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+{x}^{2}-2y & =64-{y}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+8x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =64 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =64+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4,b=1$ and $r=9,$ and\n\n$$\na+b+r=-4+1+9=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a258d3a2e0e27b7c226e21ede81ca9fb0a114c45cb76137c083288ea969fc75"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-15304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}-x+{y}^{2}-4y=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x+{y}^{2}-4y & =-2 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =-2 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-2+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(y-2)}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(y-2)}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$ and its radius is $\\frac{3}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a258d3a2e0e27b7c226e21ede81ca9fb0a114c45cb76137c083288ea969fc75"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-\\frac{1}{2},-2)$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{1}{2},2)$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(2,\\frac{1}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(\\frac{1}{2},-2)$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "center: $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$, radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+3x+{y}^{2}-y=-\\frac{9}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3x+{y}^{2}-y & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+3x)+({y}^{2}-y) & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}y+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =-\\frac{9}{4}+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}y+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-\\frac{3}{2}))}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ and its radius is $\\frac{1}{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a258d3a2e0e27b7c226e21ede81ca9fb0a114c45cb76137c083288ea969fc75"} {"question" "q-76370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979803/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e504519cd33d69a6d659670e0151b87b381ea93b83b4ae1aa8e0eec744656c1"} {"question" "q-76370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "center: $(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "center: $(\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}